WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.150
Notation on staves

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:07.783
Open the notation window with the Notate button.

3
00:00:07.883 --> 00:00:14.483
Give the piece a title and choose the time signature, key and tempo.

4
00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:20.250
The grid rounds your playing: eighths give a calm score.

5
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:26.117
The second page holds the staves: one per hand and one for the pedal.

6
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:34.250
Link each staff to a MIDI channel: click Learn and play one key on the keyboard for that hand.

7
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.450
Do the same for the left hand and the pedal.

8
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.683
Each staff now has its own channel. Click Create piece.

9
00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:52.683
Step input: switch on Step input and play the notes one by one; the cursor moves on by itself.

10
00:00:52.783 --> 00:00:58.617
Play a chord simply by pressing all its keys at once.

11
00:00:58.717 --> 00:01:06.017
Undo (Ctrl+Z) takes the input back step by step.

12
00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:12.650
Or record live: click Record and play. Right hand, left hand and pedal land on their own staves at once.

13
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:18.883
The line below the staves shows which staff catches which channel.

14
00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:25.650
Click Record again to stop: the piece is there, neatly aligned to the grid.

15
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:33.517
Click a note to select it and adjust it, for example up a semitone and back down.

16
00:01:33.617 --> 00:01:39.650
Save the piece via File, or export it as MusicXML, MIDI or PDF.

17
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.950
Klavar notation? See the video Notation in klavar.
